---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.tsx";
---

<Layout>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <div class="mb-6" style="padding-right: 40px;">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 mb-2">
      <h1 class="font-medium m-0 text-heading" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">
        &gt; halvard_mørstad
      </h1>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/halvardssm"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          aria-label="GitHub"
        >
          <Icon name="brand-github" size={16} color="var(--color-dim)" />
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/halvard-mørstad-4b8b13144/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          aria-label="LinkedIn"
        >
          <Icon name="brand-linkedin" size={16} color="var(--color-dim)" />
        </a>
        <a href="mailto:halvard@morstad.eu" aria-label="Email">
          <Icon name="mail" size={16} color="var(--color-dim)" />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      // Cloud and infrastructure engineer, occasionally full-stack.<br />
      // Ten years in, still enjoy picking up a stack I've never touched.<br />
      // These days that extends to leading the people who build alongside me.<br />
      // Comfortable down to the metal, Rust, Go, and the occasional x86 detour.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- CTA buttons -->
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2.5 mb-8">
    <a
      href="mailto:halvard@morstad.eu"
      class="btn-primary"
      style="padding: 0.5rem 1rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; display: inline-flex; align-items: center;"
    >
      $ lets_talk()
    </a>
    <a
      href="/work"
      class="btn-outline"
      style="padding: 0.5rem 0.875rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; display: inline-flex; align-items: center;"
    >
      cd ./work
    </a>
    <a
      href="/blog"
      class="btn-outline"
      style="padding: 0.5rem 0.875rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; display: inline-flex; align-items: center;"
    >
      cd ./blog
    </a>
  </div>

  <!-- Link to non-technical version -->
  <a
    href="/about"
    class="btn-outline"
    style="padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; text-decoration: none;"
  >
    <Icon name="click" size={28} color="var(--color-link)" />
    <span
      >I can also present to your&nbsp;<br />non-technical
      stakeholders&nbsp;<br />see that view here</span
    >
  </a>

  <!-- Ways to work with me -->
  <h2 class="m-0 mb-2.5 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">
    // ways to work with me
  </h2>
  <section
    class="grid gap-2.5 mb-8"
    style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr));"
  >
    <div class="card" style="padding: 1rem;">
      <Icon name="code" size={16} color="#85b7eb" />
      <h3
        class="font-medium m-0 mt-2.5 mb-1 text-heading"
        style="font-size: 0.875rem;"
      >
        Hands-on engineering
      </h3>
      <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6;">
        Cloud, infra, and full-stack builds you can hand off with confidence.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="padding: 1rem;">
      <Icon name="bulb" size={16} color="#f0997b" />
      <h3
        class="font-medium m-0 mt-2.5 mb-1 text-heading"
        style="font-size: 0.875rem;"
      >
        Advisory and greenfield builds
      </h3>
      <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6;">
        Pick the right stack, validate before committing budget, or find what's
        broken.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="padding: 1rem;">
      <Icon name="users" size={16} color="#97c459" />
      <h3
        class="font-medium m-0 mt-2.5 mb-1 text-heading"
        style="font-size: 0.875rem;"
      >
        Fractional leadership
      </h3>
      <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6;">
        Interim CTO work, team building, and technical strategy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- About -->
  <div class="pb-5 mt-8">
    <h2 class="m-0 mb-2 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">// about</h2>
    <p
      class="m-0 text-muted mb-3"
      style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.8;"
    >
      I'm a cloud and infrastructure engineer with a full-stack background. Ten
      years across startups and enterprise, now splitting my time between
      hands-on engineering, technical leadership, and freelance work.
    </p>
    <p class="m-0 mb-1.5 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      <span class="text-dim">// leadership</span>
      <span>
        I've led teams of up to 8 engineers, set technical direction, and
        mentored juniors. I'm comfortable as interim CTO or embedding into an
        existing team.</span
      >
    </p>
    <p class="m-0 mb-1.5 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      <span class="text-dim">// adaptability</span>
      <span>
        I pick up unfamiliar stacks quickly. I'm comfortable across the stack
        from frontend to infrastructure to low-level systems, and I've evaluated
        and adopted technologies for proof-of-concepts and greenfield projects.</span
      >
    </p>
    <p class="m-0 mb-1.5 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      <span class="text-dim">// mentoring</span>
      <span>
        I mentor junior engineers and previously taught programming. I also
        write technical content, including a course on Newline.co.</span
      >
    </p>
    <p class="m-0 mb-1.5 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      <span class="text-dim">// on ai</span>
      <span>
        AI is a tool, not a replacement. I use it to speed up scaffolding, test
        generation, and code review, but the engineer's job shifts from writing
        code to evaluating it. Get it right and you cut cost and cycle time. Get
        it wrong and you generate more rework than you saved.</span
      >
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Stats -->
  <dl
    class="flex gap-6 py-4 mb-5 m-0"
    style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);"
  >
    <div>
      <dt class="text-heading font-medium" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">~10</dt>
      <dd class="m-0 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.6875rem;">years experience</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt class="text-heading font-medium" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">8</dt>
      <dd class="m-0 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.6875rem;">engineers led</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt class="text-heading font-medium" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">25+</dt>
      <dd class="m-0 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.6875rem;">projects shipped</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <!-- Use cases -->
  <h2 class="m-0 mb-3 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">
    // what I can do for you
  </h2>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 py-3">
      <h3 class="m-0 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">// migrate to the cloud</h3>
      <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        Lift a legacy setup into containerized infra. I handle the migration,
        CI/CD, and cutover with minimal downtime.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="flex flex-col gap-1 py-3"
      style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);"
    >
      <h3 class="m-0 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">
        // ship a full-stack app
      </h3>
      <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        From a blank repo to a deployed product. I build the frontend, API, and
        database layer.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="flex flex-col gap-1 py-3"
      style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);"
    >
      <h3 class="m-0 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">
        // harden your infrastructure
      </h3>
      <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        I audit your current setup, find what's fragile, and make it reliable.
        Observability, autoscaling, and disaster recovery.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="flex flex-col gap-1 py-3"
      style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);"
    >
      <h3 class="m-0 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">
        // build a greenfield service
      </h3>
      <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        When you need to validate an idea fast. I pick the stack, build a PoC,
        and hand it off with docs.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="flex flex-col gap-1 py-3"
      style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);"
    >
      <h3 class="m-0 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">
        // lead your engineering team
      </h3>
      <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        Interim or fractional. I set technical direction, mentor your juniors,
        and keep delivery moving.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="flex flex-col gap-1 py-3"
      style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);"
    >
      <h3 class="m-0 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">
        // evaluate a new stack
      </h3>
      <p class="m-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        Before you commit budget, I prototype with the candidate technologies and
        give you a grounded recommendation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer class="pt-3.5" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);">
    <p class="m-0 text-dim" style="font-size: 0.6875rem;">© halvard mørstad</p>
  </footer>
</Layout>
